# Research Question

For a tree T on n vertices, define

```math
q=\lceil\sqrt n\rceil.
```

Let n2(T) be the number of degree-2 vertices and b(T) the exact burning number.

The conjecture is

```math
n_2(T)\le 2q-2 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad b(T)\le q.
```

At n = 19,

```math
q=\lceil\sqrt{19}\rceil=5,
```

so a genuine counterexample must satisfy

```math
n_2(T)\le8
```

and

```math
b(T)\ge6.
```

Therefore the ONLY target is:

```math
\boxed{n=19,\qquad n_2(T)\le8,\qquad b(T)\ge6.}
```

